# Blackjack API

Reactive API for a Blackjack game developed with Java 21, Spring Boot WebFlux, and a hexagonal architecture.

---

## Description

This project implements a REST API for playing Blackjack.

It allows you to:
- create a game
- check the game status
- play (HIT / STAND)
- delete a game
- rename players
- get player rankings

---

## Technologies Used

- Java 2.1
- Spring Boot 3
- Spring WebFlux (reactive)
- Maven
- JUnit 5 + Mockito
- Swagger / OpenAPI (Springdoc)
- Docker (Dockerfile included)

---

## Architecture

A hexagonal architecture has been implemented, separating:

### Domain
Pure business logic:
- Game
- Player
- Hand, Deck, Card
- GameStatus, PlayType

### Application
Use cases:
- CreateGame
- PlayGame
- GetGame
- DeleteGame
- RenamePlayer
- GetRanking

### Infrastructure
- Controllers (REST API)
- In-memory repositories
- Swagger
- Global Error Handling

---

## Main Endpoints

### Game
- `POST /game/new`
- `GET /game/{id}`
- `POST /game/{id}/play`
- `DELETE /game/{id}/delete`

### Player
- `PUT /player/{playerId}`

### Ranking
- `GET /ranking`

### Health
- `GET /health`

---

## Swagger

Available at:

http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html

---

## Running the Project

### Compiling

```bash
./mvnw clean compile

On Windows:

.\mvnw.cmd clean compile
Tests
./mvnw test
Run the application
./mvnw spring-boot:run
Current Persistence

The project currently uses in-memory repositories:

Data is retained only while the app is running; upon restart, it is lost.
Important Note

The architecture is designed to integrate:

MongoDB (for Game)
MySQL (for Player)

but these were not implemented due to time constraints.

Ranking

The ranking is calculated using:

score = (wins * 3) + draws
Error Handling

A GlobalExceptionHandler was implemented that returns errors in JSON format.

Docker

Included:

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
Build
docker build -t blackjack-api .

Run
docker run -p 8080:8080 blackjack-api
Note

Full validation of Docker execution could not be performed due to a connection issue while downloading the base image.

Tests

Tests have been implemented in:

Domain (Game, Hand, Deck)
Services
Controllers

All tests passed successfully.

Limitations / Known Bugs
In-memory persistence (no real database)
Docker failed to run completely due to a network issue (not code-related)
No authentication or security
No advanced validation on all endpoints
Some responses are not fully typed for production
